# Tier-0 eval question set (issue #54, WS-A PR 4/8).
#
# Schema: one JSON object per line (comment lines start with '#'):
#   id                        unique stable identifier (string)
#   question                  natural-language question (must not begin with a greeting
#                             keyword - the engine's greeting bypass skips retrieval)
#   expected_doc_id           filename of the corpus document that answers the question
#                             (eval/corpus/<expected_doc_id>); null for out-of-corpus rows
#   expected_page             null for .md-sourced corpora (no page concept); populated
#                             once pdf/pptx fixtures land
#   expected_training_slide_id  STAYS null until the Storyline extractor (D1, issue #77)
#                             exists - follow-up note: populate slide ids only after #77
#                             ships doc-to-slide links (see issue #54 required scope)
#   category                  taxonomy value documented in eval/README.md
#
# Out-of-corpus rows (expected_doc_id null, category "out-of-corpus") measure abstain
# accuracy: the backend SHOULD decline to answer them. Keep at least 5 such rows and keep
# the in-corpus/out-of-corpus ratio roughly 90/10 for this tier-0 set.
